\frametitle{Multi-GPU was almost free}\framesubtitle {one rank $\to $ one GPU --- the FMS/MPI decomposition already existed}
  \begin{cookiecode}[title={the entire multi-GPU enablement}]{Fortran}
call MPI_COMM_RANK( mpp_comm_private, pe,   error )
call MPI_COMM_SIZE( mpp_comm_private, npes, error )
!$    call omp_set_default_device (pe)
!$acc set device_num(pe)
  \end{cookiecode}
  \begin{itemize}
    \item Each MPI rank binds to its own GPU (\texttt{pe} $\to$ device) --- that is the whole change.
    \item Domain decomposition and halo exchange were \textbf{already there} in FMS; nothing else to add.
    \item GPUDirect lets the existing \texttt{pass\_*} halos travel device-to-device.
  \end{itemize}
